  "text_input": "Patient was apparently alright 1 year back when she started complaining of her symptoms of joint pain. Started 1 year ago insidious onset joint pain involving both knee which was bilateral & symmetrical, over the next few months pain gradually progressed to involve B/L Elbow joints & shoulder joints & also small joints of hands (like MCP/PIP joints). Patient describe the pain as chronic, persistent & non migratory, same intensity throughout the day. Not relieved by rest or aggravated by activity. No H/O Acute inflammatory flares. No History of significant morning stiffness, no redness or marked warmth over joints & no obvious deformities noted \n.Pt complain of easy fatigability since 6 months gradual onset progressive affecting her daily routine activities & temporarily relieves on taking rest.\nPt also complain of B/L lower limb swelling since 3 months. Started at the ankle region and gradually progressed upward is B/L & symmetrical. Not associated with pain, redness over the swelling.\nNo H/O - Dyspnea, Orthopnea, PND, decreased urine output, Fever",
